course: dictionary
lesson: 13586
title: Included: part of the whole
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Included means put in as part of a whole or a group. If something is included, it is already counted in the total. «Breakfast included» means the breakfast is already paid for, so you do not pay extra.
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. On a box, «Batteries not included» tells you the batteries are not in the box. Swap in "part of" and check: «Breakfast is part of the price» still makes sense, so included means part of the whole.
explain: Included also describes feelings. To feel included is to feel that you belong in a group. «Everyone was included in the game at break time» means nobody was left out.
fact: Included means put in as part of a whole or a group.
fact: «Tax included» means the tax is already counted in the price.
fact: «Batteries not included» means the batteries are not in the box.
fact: To feel included is to feel that you belong in a group.
fact: A good check is to swap in "part of" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Lunch is included in the price.» What does included mean here? | Thrown away with the rubbish | *Already counted in the price | Left out of the price | Paid for again at the till
exercise: Maya says, «Everyone was included in the game.» What does this show? | *Nobody was left out, and everyone belonged | The rules were broken | The game was cancelled | Only the tallest children could play
exercise: «Water bottles not included.» What does this sign tell you? | The box is empty | The water is free | The bottles are in the box | *The bottles are not in the box
test: «The ticket price included a drink.» What does included mean? | *Had a drink counted in the price | Had a drink from a stranger | Had a drink thrown in the bin | Had a drink that was forgotten
test: Ruby says she feels included in her new class. What does that mean? | She is sitting alone at the back | She is always late for lessons | She has to leave the class | *She belongs in the group
exam: Which sentence shows that someone belongs in a group? | «The shop was closed on Sunday.» | «The bus was late this morning.» | *«Jade was included in the choir.» | «The rain stopped at lunchtime.»
